Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive summary:

## Summary: SharedFileBrowser Context Menu Implementation

Based on my thorough search of the web app codebase, here's what I found:

### 1. **SharedFileBrowser Component Location**
- **File:** `/Users/michael/Code/cipher-box/apps/web/src/components/file-browser/SharedFileBrowser.tsx`
- **Lines 67-535:** Complete component implementation
- **Related files:** 
  - `/Users/michael/Code/cipher-box/apps/web/src/components/file-browser/ContextMenu.tsx` (shared context menu component)
  - `/Users/michael/Code/cipher-box/apps/web/src/styles/context-menu.css` (context menu styling)
  - `/Users/michael/Code/cipher-box/apps/web/src/styles/shared-browser.css` (shared view styling)

### 2. **How Context Menus Work in Shared View**

**Two-view architecture:**
- **List view** (line 179): Top-level shared items with a "SHARED BY" column
- **Folder view** (line 307): Inside a shared folder showing individual files/folders

Both views use the same `ContextMenu` component with the `readOnly={true}` prop (lines 290, 458).

**Context Menu Container (ContextMenu.tsx, line 226):**
```tsx
<div
  className="context-menu"
  role="menu"
  aria-label={isMultiSelect ? `Actions for ${selectedCount} items` : `Actions for ${item.name}`}
>
```

The CSS class `"context-menu"` with `role="menu"` is defined in `/Users/michael/Code/cipher-box/apps/web/src/styles/context-menu.css` (lines 12-22):
```css
.context-menu {
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 1100;
  min-width: 180px;
  padding: var(--spacing-xs) 0;
  background-color: var(--color-background);
  border: var(--border-thickness) solid var(--color-border);
  box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5), var(--glow-green);
}
```

### 3. **Preview Availability in Shared Files**

**YES - Preview IS available for shared files:**

The SharedFileBrowser passes `onPreview` callback in two places:

**In list view (lines 279-293):**
```tsx
{contextMenu.visible && contextMenu.item && (
  <ContextMenu
    ...
    onDownload={contextMenu.item.type === 'file' ? handleDownload : undefined}
    // No Preview shown in list view - only Download
    readOnly
    onHide={contextShareId ? handleHide : undefined}
  />
)}
```

**In folder view (lines 437-460):**
```tsx
{contextMenu.visible && contextMenu.item && (
  <ContextMenu
    ...
    onDownload={contextMenu.item.type === 'file' ? handleDownload : undefined}
    onEdit={
      contextMenu.item.type === 'file' && isTextFile(contextMenu.item.name)
        ? handleEditClick
        : undefined
    }
    onPreview={
      contextMenu.item.type === 'file' && isPreviewableFile(contextMenu.item.name)
        ? handlePreviewClick
        : undefined
    }
    readOnly
  />
)}
```

Preview dialogs imported at the top (lines 26-30):
- `ImagePreviewDialog`
- `PdfPreviewDialog`
- `AudioPlayerDialog`
- `VideoPlayerDialog`
- `TextEditorDialog` (for text preview)

### 4. **Differences: Shared vs Owned Files Context Menu**

| Action | Owned Files | Shared Files (Folder View) | Shared Files (List View) |
|--------|------------|---------------------------|------------------------|
| **Download** | ✓ | ✓ | ✗ (requires entering share) |
| **Preview** | ✓ (images, PDF, audio, video) | ✓ (images, PDF, audio, video) | ✗ |
| **Edit** | ✓ (text files only) | ✓ (text files only) | ✗ |
| **Rename** | ✓ | ✗ (read-only) | ✗ (read-only) |
| **Move** | ✓ | ✗ (read-only) | ✗ (read-only) |
| **Share** | ✓ | ✗ (read-only) | ✗ (read-only) |
| **Details** | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| **Delete** | ✓ | ✗ (read-only) | ✗ (read-only) |
| **Hide** | N/A | N/A | ✓ (removes from shared view) |

**Owned files** (FileBrowser.tsx, lines 795-799):
```tsx
onPreview={
  isFilePointer(contextMenu.item) && isPreviewableFile(contextMenu.item.name)
    ? handlePreviewClick
    : undefined
}
```

**Shared files** (SharedFileBrowser.tsx, lines 450-454):
```tsx
onPreview={
  contextMenu.item.type === 'file' && isPreviewableFile(contextMenu.item.name)
    ? handlePreviewClick
    : undefined
}
```

### 5. **Preview Handler Implementation**

Both use the same `isPreviewableFile()` utility (imported from `'../../utils/fileTypes'`) to determine if a file supports preview.

The handler routes to appropriate dialog:
```tsx
const handlePreviewClick = useCallback(() => {
  const item = contextMenu.item;
  if (!item || !isFilePointer(item)) return;
  const name = item.name;
  if (isTextFile(name)) {
    setEditorDialog({ open: true, item });
  } else if (isImageFile(name)) {
    setImagePreviewDialog({ open: true, item });
  } else if (isPdfFile(name)) {
    setPdfPreviewDialog({ open: true, item });
  } else if (isAudioFile(name)) {
    setAudioPlayerDialog({ open: true, item });
  } else if (isVideoFile(name)) {
    setVideoPlayerDialog({ open: true, item });
  }
}, [contextMenu.item]);
```

### 6. **Key Implementation Details**

- **readOnly mode** (ContextMenu.tsx, line 47-48): When `readOnly={true}`, the context menu hides Rename, Move, Delete, Edit, and Share actions
- **onHide callback** (ContextMenu.tsx, lines 373-383): Exclusive to shared view—allows users to hide shares from their list
- **List view limitation**: In list view (top-level shares), Preview/Edit aren't offered—user must double-click to enter the share first (line 136: `await navigateToShare(contextShareId)`)
- **Portal rendering** (ContextMenu.tsx, line 223): Context menu renders in a Portal to avoid z-index/overflow issues
- **Floating UI positioning** (ContextMenu.tsx, lines 107-111): Uses @floating-ui/react for edge detection and automatic repositioning

All files are absolute paths within `/Users/michael/Code/cipher-box/apps/web/src/`.

